  "content_id": "16136016",
  "title": "How do I export transactions into CSV or Quickbooks?",
  "description": "Edge can export your transaction history to use for tax purposes or personal records.\n \nFrom the main wallet screen:\n\nTap \"Assets\" located...",
  "body": "<p class=\"no-margin\">Edge can export your transaction history to use for tax purposes or personal records.</p><p class=\"no-margin\">From the main wallet screen:</p><ol><li><p class=\"no-margin\">Tap \"Assets\" located within the bottom navigation bar</p></li><li><p class=\"no-margin\">Tap on the wallet you'd like to export transactions from.</p></li><li><p class=\"no-margin\">Once inside the wallet tap on the three vertical dots located at upper right of the screen</p></li><li><p class=\"no-margin\">Tap \"Export Transactions\" and you'll have an option to export your wallet's transaction history as a QBP or CSV file. Select the date range that you'd like to export and then you can tap \"Export\" to send out to your preferred method.</p></li></ol><p class=\"no-margin\">NOTE: Edge does not send you tax documents such as 1099. Edge does not have access to user accounts.</p>",
  "author_id": 9849332,
  "state": "published",
  "created_at": 1772222666,
  "updated_at": 1772222667,
  "url": "https://support.edge.app/en/articles/13892300-how-do-i-export-transactions-into-csv-or-quickbooks"
}
